@@ -21,19 +21,28 @@ Coverage never grants execution authority. Agents may prepare work; accountable
 
 ## Development
 
-Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer and Linux with `flock`, `curl`, GNU `timeout`, and `zip`.
+Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer. The normal contributor path is cross-platform:
 
 ```sh
-npm run install:ci
+npm ci
 npm run generate:platform
 npm run validate:platform
 npm run lint
 npm test
 ```
 
-`npm test` builds the production Worker and runs contract, site-wide quality, mobile, and LedgerBench program suites. See [`TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) for the coverage matrix, focused commands, and release gates.
+`npm test` builds the production Worker and runs contract, site-wide quality, mobile, and LedgerBench program suites. `npm run test:browser` adds real Chromium and WebKit interaction tests with the pinned Playwright and axe-core development dependencies. See [`TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) for the coverage matrix and release gates.
 
-`data/open-source-platform.mjs` is the canonical source for packs, public conformance cases, and release notes. `data/ledgerbench-program.mjs` is the canonical structured Preview record for the LedgerBench measurement program.
+The current ChatGPT Sites environment has an additional hardened wrapper for its constrained Linux runtime:
+
+```sh
+npm run sites:install
+npm run sites:build
+```
+
+Those commands require Linux `flock`, `curl`, GNU `timeout`, and `/proc`; ordinary contributors and other CI providers do not.
+
+`data/open-source-platform.mjs` is the canonical source for packs, public conformance cases, and release notes. `data/ledgerbench-program.mjs` is the canonical structured Preview record for the LedgerBench measurement program. `data/release.json` is the single release/version/date descriptor used by human and machine projections.
 
 Run the deterministic Core reference harness:
 
@@ -55,7 +64,7 @@ npm run archive:source
